s default in clang.  Change-Id: Ibfbb3e631284ade53b75835bab66f481b4bab268 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/651567 Commit-Ready: Manoj Gupta &lt;manojgupta@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Manoj Gupta &lt;manojgupta@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="651567" owner_email="manojgupta@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/67/651567/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie327752c2b2980f541e091867e75ac135f870e83" commit="cf54e76454bb86e4c41deb482dc2603ac701b175" commit_message="[autotest] Exclude moblab from lab inventory management.  The moblab instances in Stierlin Ct are handled by a separate process that's separate from the standard lab inventory cron job e-mail.  So, remove the board from consideration.  BUG=chromium:757815 TEST=unit test for sanity  Change-Id: Ie327752c2b2980f541e091867e75ac135f870e83 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/647316 Commit-Ready: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@google.com&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="647316" owner_email="jrbarnette@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/16/647316/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ied5f873281646ada13c31774953566549b149024" commit="9204ced88c059bfa78a97d2652400c1b1d814e34" commit_message="cros_chrome_sdk: Continue if VM is not found.  VM image is not generated for some boards. --download-vm now prints an error message instead of failing.  BUG=chromium:762643 TEST=manual  Change-Id: Ied5f873281646ada13c31774953566549b149024 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/651886 Commit-Ready: Achuith Bhandarkar &lt;achuith@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Achuith Bhandarkar &lt;achuith@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Steven Bennetts &lt;stevenjb@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="651886" owner_email="achuith@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/86/651886/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I61aac891926b771b8511e755957f594824a2d821" commit="b8dd85b2f2575c93fe500f94d009400d6d6470fe" commit_message="FROMGIT: USB: core: Avoid race of async_completed() w/ usbdev_release()  While running reboot tests w/ a specific set of USB devices (and slub_debug enabled), I found that once every few hours my device would be crashed with a stack that looked like this:  [   14.012445] BUG: spinlock bad magic on CPU#0, modprobe/2091 [   14.012460]  lock: 0xffffffc0cb055978, .magic: ffffffc0, .owner: cryption contexts: %lu/%lu [   14.012460] /1025536097, .owner_cpu: 0 [   14.012466] CPU: 0 PID: 2091 Comm: modprobe Not tainted 4.4.79 #352 [   14.012468] Hardware name: Google Kevin (DT) [   14.012471] Call trace: [   14.012483] [&lt;....&gt;] dump_backtrace+0x0/0x160 [   14.012487] [&lt;....&gt;] show_stack+0x20/0x28 [   14.012494] [&lt;....&gt;] dump_stack+0xb4/0xf0 [   14.012500] [&lt;....&gt;] spin_dump+0x8c/0x98 [   14.012504] [&lt;....&gt;] spin_bug+0x30/0x3c [   14.012508] [&lt;....&gt;] do_raw_spin_lock+0x40/0x164 [   14.012515] [&lt;....&gt;] _raw_spin_lock_irqsave+0x64/0x74 [   14.012521] [&lt;....&gt;] __wake_up+0x2c/0x60 [   14.012528] [&lt;....&gt;] async_completed+0x2d0/0x300 [   14.012534] [&lt;....&gt;] __usb_hcd_giveback_urb+0xc4/0x138 [   14.012538] [&lt;....&gt;] usb_hcd_giveback_urb+0x54/0xf0 [   14.012544] [&lt;....&gt;] xhci_irq+0x1314/0x1348 [   14.012548] [&lt;....&gt;] usb_hcd_irq+0x40/0x50 [   14.012553] [&lt;....&gt;] handle_irq_event_percpu+0x1b4/0x3f0 [   14.012556] [&lt;....&gt;] handle_irq_event+0x4c/0x7c [   14.012561] [&lt;....&gt;] handle_fasteoi_irq+0x158/0x1c8 [   14.012564] [&lt;....&gt;] generic_handle_irq+0x30/0x44 [   14.012568] [&lt;....&gt;] __handle_domain_irq+0x90/0xbc [   14.012572] [&lt;....&gt;] gic_handle_irq+0xcc/0x18c  Investigation using kgdb() found that the wait queue that was passed into wake_up() had been freed (it was filled with slub_debug poison).  I analyzed and instrumented the code and reproduced.  My current belief is that this is happening:  1. async_completed() is called (from IRQ).  Moves &quot;as&quot; onto the    completed list. 2. On another CPU, proc_reapurbnonblock_compat() calls    async_getcompleted().  Blocks on spinlock. 3. async_completed() releases the lock; keeps running; gets blocked    midway through wake_up(). 4. proc_reapurbnonblock_compat() =&gt; async_getcompleted() gets the    lock; removes &quot;as&quot; from completed list and frees it. 5. usbdev_release() is called.  Frees &quot;ps&quot;. 6. async_completed() finally continues running wake_up().  ...but    wake_up() has a pointer to the freed &quot;ps&quot;.  The instrumentation that led me to believe this was based on adding some trace_printk() calls in a select few functions and then using kdb's &quot;ftdump&quot; at crash time.  The trace follows (NOTE: in the trace below I cheated a little bit and added a udelay(1000) in async_completed() after releasing the spinlock because I wanted it to trigger quicker):  &lt;...&gt;-2104   0d.h2 13759034us!: async_completed at start: as=ffffffc0cc638200 mtpd-2055    3.... 13759356us : async_getcompleted before spin_lock_irqsave mtpd-2055    3d..1 13759362us : async_getcompleted after list_del_init: as=ffffffc0cc638200 mtpd-2055    3.... 13759371us+: proc_reapurbnonblock_compat: free_async(ffffffc0cc638200) mtpd-2055    3.... 13759422us+: async_getcompleted before spin_lock_irqsave mtpd-2055    3.... 13759479us : usbdev_release at start: ps=ffffffc0cc042080 mtpd-2055    3.... 13759487us : async_getcompleted before spin_lock_irqsave mtpd-2055    3.... 13759497us!: usbdev_release after kfree(ps): ps=ffffffc0cc042080 &lt;...&gt;-2104   0d.h2 13760294us : async_completed before wake_up(): as=ffffffc0cc638200  To fix this problem we can just move the wake_up() under the ps-&gt;lock. There should be no issues there that I'm aware of.  BUG=None TEST=No more of this kind of crash in reboot tests  Change-Id: I61aac891926b771b8511e755957f594824a2d821 Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Acked-by: Alan Stern &lt;stern@rowland.harvard.edu&gt; Cc: stable &lt;stable@vger.kernel.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman &lt;gregkh@linuxfoundation.org&gt; (cherry picked from git.kernel.org gregkh/usb.git usb-next  commit ed62ca2f4f51c17841ea39d98c0c409cb53a3e10) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/641357 Reviewed-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="641357" owner_email="dianders@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/57/641357/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I33f73f19d93be3ad5a104825c71a47ad9e7016a8" commit="291fe4fb6992df7d469ddd498d1e2e6dc7350361" commit_message="autotest: fix the case that metrics key is None.  BUG=chromium:762237 TEST=Ran unittest.  Change-Id: I33f73f19d93be3ad5a104825c71a47ad9e7016a8 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/653245 Commit-Ready: Xixuan Wu &lt;xixuan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Xixuan Wu &lt;xixuan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shuqian Zhao &lt;shuqianz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="653245" owner_email="xixuan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/45/653245/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ibf8f3f319e62daf956073471e72e284689112e26" commit="721b52eb8d4dce620432a98f3b72ed63ad7e6f9f" commit_message="evtest: Add usage info to safe mode patch  This cl updates the --safe mode patch with usage info and patch description.  BUG=chromium:762297 TEST=local build and evtest  Change-Id: Ibf8f3f319e62daf956073471e72e284689112e26 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/653207 Commit-Ready: Jingkui Wang &lt;jkwang@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Jingkui Wang &lt;jkwang@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="653207" owner_email="jkwang@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/07/653207/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia9cb21d8a85241be2d6a675eb4b2c1186aef9d8a" commit="9f1eed4e9995fb3fd17e12009fc60e155dbea48b" commit_message="ISH: inclued header for sleep mask  Fix errors due to missing definition of enable_sleep/disable_sleep.  BUG=None BRANCH=master Test='make -j buildall'  Change-Id: Ia9cb21d8a85241be2d6a675eb4b2c1186aef9d8a Signed-off-by: Kyoung Kim &lt;kyoung.il.kim@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/651139 Commit-Ready: Kyoung Il Kim &lt;kyoung.il.kim@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Kyoung Il Kim &lt;kyoung.il.kim@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="651139" owner_email="kyoung.il.kim@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/39/651139/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If45017627c7b22d95af1588ef989ed13794e6452" commit="1468c6b064ef8926097749e8aa4d5c05f88df1e7" commit_message="master-paladin: Cancel slaves on self-destruct  Create a library function CancelBuilds, called on self-destruct of a  master build to cancel all slave builds. Refactor CancelObsoleteBuilds to call this as well, for the shared code. Create mock patching to route around this path in existing tests. Copy and adapt tests from CancelObsoleteSlaveBuilds to also cover CancelBuilds. Add tests for type-checking to ensure JSON serializability of  buildbucket_ids, preventing the failure that required a revert.  BUG=chromium:753189 TEST=cbuildbot/run_tests  Change-Id: If45017627c7b22d95af1588ef989ed13794e6452 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/644102 Commit-Ready: Jacob Kopczynski &lt;jkop@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Jacob Kopczynski &lt;jkop@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ningning Xia &lt;nxia@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Jacob Kopczynski &lt;jkop@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="644102" owner_email="jkop@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/02/644102/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Iecc4a1e302ff72a9763b9ca6dac7dc44d588a6d1" commit="0e4a88e59e20e34ab477f81cb4ac0a4a770d9bc2" commit_message="UPSTREAM: tcp: initialize rcv_mss to TCP_MIN_MSS instead of 0  When tcp_disconnect() is called, inet_csk_delack_init() sets icsk-&gt;icsk_ack.rcv_mss to 0. This could potentially cause tcp_recvmsg() =&gt; tcp_cleanup_rbuf() =&gt; __tcp_select_window() call path to have division by 0 issue. So this patch initializes rcv_mss to TCP_MIN_MSS instead of 0.  BUG=chromium:762451 TEST=Build and run  Change-Id: Iecc4a1e302ff72a9763b9ca6dac7dc44d588a6d1 Reported-by: Andrey Konovalov  &lt;andreyknvl@google.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Wei Wang &lt;weiwan@google.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Eric Dumazet &lt;edumazet@google.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Neal Cardwell &lt;ncardwell@google.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Yuchung Cheng &lt;ycheng@google.com&gt; Signed-off-by: David S. Miller &lt;davem@davemloft.net&gt; Signed-off-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 499350a5a6e) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/652667 Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="652667" owner_email="groeck@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/67/652667/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iea728ec987440597386efa1fdaa38c7eba2c9265" commit="924a5c3baad1339dd27eaa1d52eb6de6009772fe" commit_message="cr50_test: add function to get the state  Add a function to get the state. Make the state into a dict, so this is easier.  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=firmware_Cr50Update  Change-Id: Iea728ec987440597386efa1fdaa38c7eba2c9265 Signed-off-by: Mary Ruthven &lt;mruthven@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/648627 Reviewed-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="648627" owner_email="mruthven@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/27/648627/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="9917.0.0-rc1"/></manifest>